+# USCL fork — EA Sports online (Blaze 3.x "heat2")
+This fork extends the server beyond Skate 3 to revive **EA Sports** online play on RPCS3.
+Skate 3 and NBA Jam speak Blaze 2.x ("heat1"); the EA Sports titles (NHL 15, Madden 25,
+and the FIFA/Madden/NHL family) speak Blaze 3.x ("heat2"), with a different TDF encoding
+and login handshake.
+
+**Status:** NHL 15 now **logs in and connects to the EA servers** (the online ticker plays
+and it reaches "Retrieving data from server"), using a fully reverse-engineered heat2 login
+flow — TLS (SSLv3/RC4), RPCN ticket validation, the real `ConsoleLoginResponse`, and the
+`UserAuthenticated` notification that completes login. One remaining client-side crash during
+data retrieval is fully diagnosed and server-fixable.
+
+**→ See [`docs/EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md`](docs/EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md)** for the complete
+protocol write-up, the login handshake, the components, the live test harness, the PS3-EBOOT
+disassembly toolchain, and exactly how to pick the remaining work back up.
+Tooling: [`tools/ea-sports/`](tools/ea-sports/).
+
