+# EA Sports online (Blaze 3.x "heat2") — NHL 15 / Madden 25
+
+This fork extends the Skate 3 Blaze server to revive EA Sports online play on RPCS3.
+Skate 3 and NBA Jam speak **Blaze 2.x ("heat1")**; the EA Sports titles (NHL 15,
+Madden 25, and the whole FIFA/Madden/NHL family) speak **Blaze 3.x ("heat2")**, a
+different wire encoding and a different login handshake.
+
+**Status (2026-11-09):** NHL 15 **logs in and connects to the EA servers** — the online
+music ticker plays and it reaches *"Retrieving data from server"*. It then hits one
+remaining **client-side crash** during data retrieval, which is **fully diagnosed and
+server-fixable** (not an emulator bug — see §6). Everything needed to finish it is below.
+
+Branch: `uscl-nbajam-work`. Key commits: `f06b66a` (heat2 encoder), `3e1a2db` (heat2
+decoder), `bb3ea81` (handshake tests), `a2ff48c`/`53c4767` (login response),
+`4e51434` (UserAuthenticated — login completes), `afab422` (Stats component).
+
+---
+
+## 1. heat1 vs heat2
+
+| | Blaze 2.x "heat1" | Blaze 3.x "heat2" |
+|---|---|---|
+| Games | Skate 3, NBA Jam | NHL 15 (BlazeSDK 3.19), Madden 25 (13.3), FIFA, etc. |
+| TDF wire | high-nibble length typing | `[3-byte tag][1-byte type][value]`, little-endian varints |
+| Login | `login` / postAuth | `ps3Login` (cmd 200) + `UserAuthenticated` notification |
+
+**heat2 TDF** (see `Blaze/Tdf/Heat2Writer.cs` + `Heat2Reader.cs`): each field is
+`[3-byte tag][1-byte type][value]`. Types: `0=int` (LE varint), `1=string`, `2=blob`,
+`3=struct` (0x00 terminator), `4=list`, `5=map`, `6=union`. A connection is flagged
+heat2 in `PreAuthHandler` by scanning the preAuth payload for the BlazeSDK tag
+`8B 39 2B` followed by an ASCII major version `>= 3`. `BlazeMessage.CreateModelFromRequest`
+picks the codec from that flag.
+
+> **Known encoder bug:** `TdfUtils.EncodeTdfTag` mis-encodes **digit-leading tags**
+> (`(0x20 | (c & 0x1F))` yields `'Q'` for `'1'`; the correct Blaze code is `c - 0x20`).
+> All-letter tags are fine. Avoid digit tags (e.g. `1CON`) or fix the encoder first.
+
+---
+
+## 2. The login handshake (SOLVED)
+
+Full flow, all working:
+
+```
+Client → gosredirector (TLS)  getServerInstance   → returns Blaze host:port (heat2 reply)
+Client → Blaze (TLS)          preAuth (Util/7)    → flags heat2
+                              fetchClientConfig (Util/1) × N  (OSDK_* sections)
+                              ps3Login (Auth/200)  → ConsoleLoginResponse
+Server →                      UserAuthenticated (UserSessions/8)   ← THE login-completion gate
+                              UserAdded (UserSessions/2)
+                              UserUpdated (UserSessions/5)
+Client →                      postAuth (Util/8), updateNetworkInfo (UserSessions/20), …
+```
+
+Four things had to be right:
+
+1. **TLS.** NHL's ProtoSSL only speaks **SSLv3 + RC4**, which OpenSSL 3.x removed. The
+   stock proxy silently broke. Fix: `tlsproxy_legacy.py` terminates TLS with
+   **tlslite-ng** (pure-Python, keeps SSLv3/RC4) and monkeypatches tlslite's OID table
+   to accept the forged EA cert's `rsaEncryption` sig-alg. Run on port 42127 with
+   `PYTHONPATH=<pylib>`. See §5.
+
+2. **Ticket validation.** Our self-hosted rpcn signs NPTickets with its **own** key, but
+   the Blaze server hard-codes the official RPCN public key. Fix: set **`HostTicketKey`**
+   in `settings.json` to our rpcn's uncompressed public point (114 hex, `04`+X+Y, derived
+   from rpcn's `ticket_private.pem`). `Ps3LoginHandler` accepts a ticket signed by the
+   official key **or** `HostTicketKey`. Expiry hard-reject was also relaxed (our tickets
+   have ~20-min TTL; idling at the menu expires them).
+
+3. **ps3Login response = the real `ConsoleLoginResponse`.** The response type for
+   `ps3Login` (200) is `ConsoleLoginResponse` (confirmed in ZamboniDevelopment/BlazeSDK).
+   Shape: `AGUP, SPAM, LDHT, NTOS, PRIV, SESS, TSUI, THST, TURI`, where
+   `SESS = SessionInfo{BUID, MAIL, FRST, LLOG, PDTL, KEY, UID}` and
+   **`PDTL = PersonaDetails{DSNM, XREF, XTYP, LAST, PID, STAS}`**. The earlier DS2-derived
+   guess used `PNAM/DPTS/EXID` — **the SDK couldn't read its own persona and logged
+   straight back out.** The persona-name tag is **`DSNM`**. See `Blaze3LoginResponse.cs`.
+
+4. **`UserAuthenticated` (UserSessions notification 8) — THE gate.** After `ps3Login`
+   the real SDK blocks until the server pushes the **local** user's session as
+   `UserSessions NotifyUserAuthenticated` (Id **8**). Without it the client shows
+   *"connecting to the EA servers…"*, pings a couple of times, then sends `logout` (70).
+   `NotifyUserAdded` (2) is for **foreign** personas only, **not** the local login.
+   Send order after the login reply: **UserAuthenticated(8) → UserAdded(2) → UserUpdated(5)**.
+   Payload of UserAuthenticated = `UserSessionLoginInfo` (see `UserAuthenticated.cs`):
+   `ALOC, BUID, DSNM, FRST, KEY, LAST, LLOG, MAIL, NASP="ps3", PID, PLAT=2 (PS3), UID,
+   USTP, XREF` (`1CON` omitted — digit-tag encoder bug, defaults to 0 anyway).
+
+Shapes 3 and 4 were reverse-engineered from the **FIFA 17 PS3 server**
+(`ceinydO/fifa17-ps3-online`) — the single most useful Blaze-3.x-PS3 reference (§7).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Components implemented for heat2
+
+| Component (wire id) | Command | Handler | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Authentication (1) | ps3Login (200) | `Ps3LoginHandler` | ConsoleLoginResponse + 3 notifications |
+| UserSessions (30722) | updateNetworkInfo (20) | `UpdateNetworkInfoHandler` | → `NotifyExtendedDataUpdated` (clears the connecting spinner) |
+| UserSessions (30722) | notifications 2/5/8 | `NotifyUserAdded`, `UserUpdated`, `UserAuthenticated` | post-login set |
+| **Stats (7)** | **getKeyScopesMap (15)** | **`GetKeyScopesMap`** | typed `KeyScopes{KSIT: map<string,KeyScopeItem>}`; the client derefs KSIT unconditionally, so the field must exist even empty. **Shared across all EA Sports.** |
+| Util (9) | preAuth(7), fetchClientConfig(1), postAuth(8), getTelemetryServer(5) | existing | config from `clientconfig/<CFID>.txt` |
+| Clubs (11) | getClubsComponentSettings (2600) | existing | |
+
+Everything else the game calls (Messaging/2, AssociationLists/6, and the game-specific
+components **2249=OsdkTicker2, 2250/2251=OSDKSeasonalPlay/OSDKTournaments**, plus 21/10,
+10/1) currently gets an **empty success** from the generic dispatcher fallback in
+`Servers/Blaze/BlazeServer.cs`. The game proceeds past all of them.
+
+`clientconfig/OSDK_TICKER.txt` was populated (`OSDK_TICKER_COUNT`, `OSDK_TICKER_POLLING_DELAY`,
+`OSDK_TICKER_NEWS_HEADER`) during debugging — harmless, left in place, but **did not** fix
+the crash (§6).
+
+---
+
+## 4. Program.cs diagnostic switch
+
+`USCL_BLAZE_LISTEN=<port>` makes the Blaze server listen on an internal port (e.g. 42101)
+so a plaintext tap can sit on the advertised `ServerPort` (42100, what `getServerInstance`
+returns) and dump the session both ways. Omit it for normal operation.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Live test harness
+
+The harness lives outside this repo; paths below are the current machine's. Ports:
+rpcn `127.0.0.3:31513`, TLS terminator `42127`, plaintext tap `42100`, Blaze server
+`42101` (internal). Chain: **NHL → TLS(42127) → tap(42100) → Blaze(42101)**, with rpcn
+minting tickets.
+
+```sh
+# 1. Blaze server (deploy dir = publish output; config/logs live here)
+cd ~/.local/share/uscl/skate3-server/server/out/linux-x64
+USCL_BLAZE_LISTEN=42101 ./"Skate Custom Server"      # listens 42101
+
+# 2. plaintext tap 42100 -> 42101 (dumps both directions)
+python3 tools/ea-sports/tap.py 42100 127.0.0.1 42101 session.bin
+
+# 3. legacy TLS terminator 42127 -> tap(42100)   (needs tlslite-ng on PYTHONPATH)
+PYTHONPATH=~/.local/share/uscl/pylib \
+  python3 <ps3-steam-np>/uscl-blaze/tls/tlsproxy_legacy.py \
+  42127 ~/.local/share/uscl/blaze-cert 127.0.0.1 42100
+
+# 4. rpcn (run FROM its working dir — needs cert.pem/rpcn.cfg/ticket_private.pem there)
+cd ~/.local/share/uscl/rpcn-probe && <rpcn-build>/target/release/rpcn
+
+# 5. NHL 15 in RPCS3 (ea-probe config, online mode)
+XDG_CONFIG_HOME=~/.local/share/uscl/rpcs3-ea-probe/config \
+XDG_CACHE_HOME=~/.local/share/uscl/rpcs3-ea-probe/cache  USCL_ONLINE=1 \
+  <rpcs3> --no-gui "<path>/NHL 15 (USA) (En,Fr).dec.iso"
+```
+
+**Deploy/rebuild the server:**
+`dotnet publish -c Release -r linux-x64 --self-contained true -o <deploy dir>`, then
+restart the server exe from the deploy dir (kill the old one first — port conflicts else).
+`ServerGlobals.BaseDirectory` = the deploy dir, so `clientconfig/` and `logs.txt` are there.
+
+**Virtual pad** (menu automation): `vpad.py <sock> x360` exposes a uinput Xbox-360 pad
+(SDL name "Xbox 360 Controller"); RPCS3 input config binds Player 1 to it. Drive it over the
+unix socket: `printf 'press A 120' | socat - UNIX-CONNECT:<sock>` (buttons A/B/X/Y/START/…,
+`dpad UP|DOWN|…`). Screenshots: `grim -o DP-1 shot.png` (NHL renders on monitor DP-1).
+
+**Decode a capture:** `tools/ea-sports/decode_heat2.py session.bin` decodes framed
+`--- C>S N bytes ---` hex blocks into component/command + TDF fields.
+
+---
+
+## 6. The remaining crash (fully diagnosed, server-fixable)
+
+After the full online bootstrap, NHL's **main PPU thread null-derefs** at a **"Retrieving
+data from server"** screen: `VM: Access violation reading location 0x0` at PC
+**`0x008b1aec`**, deterministic (~0:01:29 every boot). **The Blaze session stays healthy**
+(keeps ping/ponging) — it's the *game* crashing, not a disconnect.
+
+**Root cause (from disassembly):** the function at `0x8b1aa0` is "update the ticker
+subsystem" (one of 16 subsystems updated in a loop at caller `0x82b720`). It does
+`stgm_manager->lookup("O_SG_TCKR")` → returns **null** → dereferences it. `"stgm"`
+(immediate `0x7374676d`) is a central settings/registry manager (97 refs, so it *is*
+initialized); only the **ticker settings group `O_SG_TCKR`** is missing. The five groups
+are `O_SG_NRAD/QMSG/SYSS/TCKR/USER`. The group is keyed by its string in the manager's
+internal map (static string-ptr slot `0x2276164`, 4 refs, all reads).
+
+**Ruled out (each an empirical live test, crash byte-identical):**
+- Stats `getKeyScopesMap` response content.
+- `OSDK_TICKER` fetchClientConfig content (served 3 real fields — group still not created).
+- **RPCS3 recompiler bug**: tested `PPU Decoder = Interpreter (static)` — crashes
+  **identically**. So it is **real game logic**, not emulation. **Server-fixable.**
+
+**Next steps (pick up here):**
+1. **Cheapest — make the game skip the ticker.** Return an error (e.g.
+   `OSDKTICKER2_ERR_NOT_REGISTERED`) for the `OsdkTicker2` component (2249) instead of
+   empty success, so the game disables the ticker instead of asserting the group exists.
+   EA games routinely degrade gracefully when a component is unavailable. One code change
+   + one reboot. "Ticker disabled, online menu reachable" is a fine outcome.
+2. **Proper — create the group.** RE the `OsdkTicker2` `RegisterResponse` (the game calls
+   2249/1 + 2249/2 right before the crash; we return empty) and return it populated so the
+   game creates `O_SG_TCKR`. Deeper: the create-vs-skip decision forks through the ticker
+   init fn `0x8b0d54` (registers via `vtable[8]` with `"O_SG_TCKR"`) and two lookup sites
+   (`0x8b1694`, crash `0x8b1ad4`). Same depth as FIFA17's unsolved `0x08C9`.
+
+**Madden 25** hits the same *class* of crash earlier (FGGameSim PPU null-deref ~52s) — very
+likely the same "real missing data" problem, now that the shared login path works.
+
+### Disassembly toolchain (reusable for any PS3 game)
+
+```sh
+# extract EBOOT.BIN from a (decrypted) ISO
+xorriso -osirrox on -indev <iso> -extract /PS3_GAME/USRDIR/EBOOT.BIN ./EBOOT.BIN
+# decrypt the SELF with RPCS3 itself (no scetool needed) -> EBOOT.elf (PowerPC64)
+<rpcs3> --decrypt ./EBOOT.BIN
+# system objdump has NO PPC support; use capstone (CS_ARCH_PPC | CS_MODE_64 | CS_MODE_BIG_ENDIAN)
+python3 tools/ea-sports/ppc_analyze.py EBOOT.elf disas <vaddr> <count>
+python3 tools/ea-sports/ppc_analyze.py EBOOT.elf xref  <const>          # find lis/ori sites
+```
+
+Segment map: the code LOAD segment is `vaddr 0x10000 → file 0x0`, so **file offset =
+vaddr − 0x10000**. `ppc_analyze.py` hard-codes this; update it for a different binary.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Reference material
+
+- **`ceinydO/fifa17-ps3-online`** — FIFA 17 on RPCS3, same era/SDK. The best Blaze-3.x-PS3
+  reference: exact shapes for `UserAuthenticated` (UserSessionLoginInfo), `NotifyUserAdded`,
+  `UserUpdated`, `KeyScopes`, `UpdateHardwareFlags`, and extensive Ghidra notes on the
+  game-specific `0x08C9` component. Clone it and read `fifa17srv/blaze.py`.
+- **`ZamboniDevelopment/BlazeSDK`** — decompiled real BlazeSDK (Blaze2SDK + Blaze3SDK) with
+  JSON component/command definitions and the authoritative TDF structs. Use it to confirm
+  response types (`ps3Login → ConsoleLoginResponse`, etc.) and member tags.
+- **`lowlevelmetal/open-ds2-server`** — Dead Space 2 PS3 Blaze server. Useful but a looser
+  homebrew reimplementation (its persona tags were the wrong `PNAM/DPTS` lead — trust the
+  decompiled SDK over it).
