+## EA Sports (Blaze 3.x "heat2") additions
+
+This fork supports Blaze 3.x clients (NHL 15, Madden 25) alongside the Skate 3 / NBA Jam
+Blaze 2.x path. The relevant pieces:
+
+* **`Blaze/Tdf/Heat2Writer.cs` + `Heat2Reader.cs`** — the Blaze 3.x TDF codec
+  (`[3-byte tag][1-byte type][value]`, LE varints). `BlazeMessage.CreateModelFromRequest`
+  selects heat1 vs heat2 from a per-connection flag set in `PreAuthHandler`.
+* **`Blaze/Components/Authentication/Handlers/Ps3LoginHandler.cs`** — `ps3Login` (200) for
+  heat2: validates the RPCN ticket (official key **or** `HostTicketKey`), returns the real
+  `ConsoleLoginResponse` (`Blaze3LoginResponse.cs`), then pushes the post-login notifications
+  `UserAuthenticated(8) → UserAdded(2) → UserUpdated(5)` that complete the SDK's login.
+* **`Blaze/Components/UserSessions/Notifications/`** — `UserAuthenticated.cs` (the
+  login-completion signal), `NotifyUserAdded.cs`, `UserUpdated.cs`, `NotifyExtendedDataUpdated.cs`.
+* **`Blaze/Components/Stats/`** + **`Blaze/Routers/StatsRouter.cs`** — wire component 7
+  (Stats), `getKeyScopesMap` (15) → typed `KeyScopes` reply. Shared across EA Sports titles.
+* **`clientconfig/<CFID>.txt`** — key=value config served by `fetchClientConfig` (next to the
+  server exe, i.e. `ServerGlobals.BaseDirectory`).
+
+The full protocol write-up, login handshake, test harness, and the one remaining (diagnosed,
+server-fixable) NHL crash are documented in **[`EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md`](EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md)**.
