+# EA Sports (Blaze 3.x heat2) tooling
+
+Helper scripts for bringing up and debugging EA Sports online. See
+[`../../docs/EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md`](../../docs/EA-Sports-Blaze3-heat2.md) for the
+full picture.
+
+- **`tap.py LPORT BHOST BPORT [OUTFILE]`** — a plaintext man-in-the-middle tap. Listens on
+  `LPORT`, forwards to `BHOST:BPORT`, and dumps every Blaze frame both ways to `OUTFILE` as
+  `--- C>S N bytes ---` / `--- S>C N bytes ---` hex blocks. Sit it between the TLS terminator
+  and the real Blaze port to read the whole session in the clear.
+
+- **`decode_heat2.py capture.bin [...]`** — decodes the `C>S` request frames in a `tap.py`
+  capture into `component/command` + the top-level TDF field names (heat2 encoding). Handy
+  for seeing what the client asked for and in what order.
+
+- **`ppc_analyze.py EBOOT.elf disas|xref <arg> [count]`** — targeted PowerPC64 (big-endian)
+  analysis of a **decrypted** PS3 `EBOOT.elf` (decrypt the SELF with `rpcs3 --decrypt`).
+  `disas <vaddr> <count>` disassembles; `xref <const>` finds `lis`/`ori` sites that build a
+  32-bit constant (e.g. a 4-char tag). Needs [capstone](https://pypi.org/project/capstone/)
+  (`pip install capstone`, ideally in a venv). The code segment maps `vaddr 0x10000 → file 0x0`
+  (file offset = vaddr − 0x10000); edit the constants at the top of the file for a different
+  binary.
